{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_paper", "label": "Indexing Without Prediction (paper)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prepared for independent review, and it names its own weakest points: readers checking the work are asked to attack \u00a76.4 (offset coordinates) and \u00a74.2 (the maximality caveat) first."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_lambda_8", "label": "\u039b\u2088, the Eight-Axis Closed Distributive Lattice", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_theorem_12_1", "label": "Theorem 12.1 \u2014 Join, Meet and Comparability Are Definable from the Coordinates", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every lattice-theoretic quantity is a function of the coordinates, so it can restate them but never exceed them. The theorem is indifferent to dimension (\u039b\u2081\u2081 is as constrained as \u039b\u2088) and to faithfulness \u2014 perfecting the index moves nothing, which is why the predictive boundary did not shift by one cell when the index was improved to exactness."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_theorem_4_1_maximality", "label": "Theorem 4.1 \u2014 Maximality under Derivation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No ninth axis can be derived from the eight electronic coordinates: any function whose graph preserves closure must be a monotone function of a single coordinate, hence redundant. Proven for products of chains and verified but not proven beyond them \u2014 the caveat \u00a74.2 states plainly."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_admissibility_condition", "label": "Admissibility Condition x \u2264 \u03c6(y) with \u03c6 Non-Decreasing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_four_rules_bracketing", "label": "The Four Rules of the Bracketing Method", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Interiority, the interpolation variable read off T = Z\u00b2R/\u03bd\u00b2, deductive bracket reported separately from the point estimate, and uncertainty from a locally fitted Ritz expansion. Each rule is justified by ablation: violating interiority takes rms 248 \u2192 928 cm\u207b\u00b9, the wrong variable 248 \u2192 589, pooled \u03c3 inflates \u00b11\u03c3 coverage to 96.2 %, and a collapsed orbital trebles median error."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_deductive_containment", "label": "Deductive Containment, the Only Escape from Theorem 12.1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bracket is not a function of the coordinates but an entailment of the order given monotonicity, so it escapes the theorem that traps every lattice quantity. That is why the bracket never failed in 295 cells while every point-estimate claim in the work required qualification."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_six_mechanisms", "label": "Six Mechanisms of Predictive Failure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rank aggregation (rank is a sum over axes and discards which axis moved), comparability (a theorem given monotonicity, not a finding), zero-shot subset selection (matched exactly by an unfitted +1-weight sum), closure-as-existence (spectroscopists measure downward-closed regions by construction), join-based mixing (62 % of pairs have no upper bound at all), and a derived ordinal coordinate (every component is a coordinate)."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_295_interior_cells", "label": "295 Interior Cells, Bracket Exact in Every One", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_extension_by_independent_quantities", "label": "Extension by Independent Quantities (\u039b\u2089\u2013\u039b\u2081\u2081)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_multi_target_extension_failure", "label": "The Multi-Target Extension and Why It Fails", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Canonicalising e\u2081 \u2264 e\u2082 is free and admissible, but conservation g\u2081 + g\u2082 \u2264 q is a bound on a sum and breaks closure; dropping it restores closure at 45,690 cells. The conserving set is not a sublattice but is 'almost' a lattice, and the slot representation is not faithful."}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_offset_coordinates", "label": "Offset Coordinates: Faithful but Not Closed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_rydberg_quantum_defect", "label": "T = Z_eff\u00b2R/\u03bd\u00b2 and the Quantum Defect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_interval_versus_point_propagation", "label": "Intervals Compose Exactly, Points Catastrophically", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Propagating point values through n \u2192 I \u2192 \u03b4 \u2192 E amplifies a 334 cm\u207b\u00b9 input error by 1.3 \u00d7 10\u2076 because dI/d\u03b4 \u2248 75,000 cm\u207b\u00b9; propagating intervals does not amplify at all, each level's width being set by the spacing of its own measured neighbours."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_paper", "target": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_lambda_8", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_paper", "target": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_theorem_12_1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/indexing-without-prediction.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_paper", "target": "recovered_indexing_without_prediction_theorem_4_1_maximality", "relation": "refer